      >>SOURCE FORMAT FREE
*> The Computer Language Benchmarks Game: reverse-complement
*> COBOL (GnuCOBOL) port by the Institut du Numerique Responsable.
*> Reads FASTA from standard input; each sequence is buffered in memory
*> that doubles as needed, then written back 60 characters per line.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. revcomp.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
FILE-CONTROL.
    SELECT IN-FILE ASSIGN TO KEYBOARD
        ORGANIZATION IS LINE SEQUENTIAL.
DATA DIVISION.
FILE SECTION.
FD IN-FILE
    RECORD IS VARYING IN SIZE FROM 0 TO 4096 CHARACTERS
    DEPENDING ON REC-LEN.
01 IN-REC            PIC X(4096).
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01 REC-LEN           PIC 9(9) COMP-5.
01 EOF-FLAG          PIC 9 VALUE 0.
   88 AT-EOF         VALUE 1.
01 HAVE-SEQ          PIC 9 VALUE 0.
01 HEADER-TEXT       PIC X(4096).
01 HEADER-LEN        PIC 9(9) COMP-5 VALUE 0.
01 SEQ-LEN           PIC 9(12) COMP-5 VALUE 0.
01 CAPACITY          PIC 9(12) COMP-5 VALUE 0.
01 NEW-CAPACITY      PIC 9(12) COMP-5.
01 START-POS         PIC 9(12) COMP-5.
01 TAIL-LEN          PIC 9(4) COMP-5.
01 SEQ-PTR           USAGE POINTER.
01 OLD-PTR           USAGE POINTER.
01 OUT-LINE          PIC X(60).
01 SEQ-BUF           PIC X(999999999) BASED.
01 OLD-BUF           PIC X(999999999) BASED.

PROCEDURE DIVISION.
MAIN-PARA.
    MOVE 1048576 TO CAPACITY
    ALLOCATE CAPACITY CHARACTERS RETURNING SEQ-PTR
    SET ADDRESS OF SEQ-BUF TO SEQ-PTR
    OPEN INPUT IN-FILE
    PERFORM UNTIL AT-EOF
        READ IN-FILE
            AT END
                SET AT-EOF TO TRUE
            NOT AT END
                PERFORM HANDLE-LINE
        END-READ
    END-PERFORM
    CLOSE IN-FILE
    IF HAVE-SEQ = 1
        PERFORM FLUSH-SEQUENCE
    END-IF
    FREE SEQ-PTR
    STOP RUN.

HANDLE-LINE.
    IF REC-LEN > 0 AND IN-REC(1:1) = ">"
        IF HAVE-SEQ = 1
            PERFORM FLUSH-SEQUENCE
        END-IF
        MOVE IN-REC(1:REC-LEN) TO HEADER-TEXT
        MOVE REC-LEN TO HEADER-LEN
        MOVE 0 TO SEQ-LEN
        MOVE 1 TO HAVE-SEQ
    ELSE
        IF REC-LEN > 0
            IF SEQ-LEN + REC-LEN > CAPACITY
                PERFORM GROW-BUFFER
            END-IF
            MOVE IN-REC(1:REC-LEN) TO SEQ-BUF(SEQ-LEN + 1:REC-LEN)
            ADD REC-LEN TO SEQ-LEN
        END-IF
    END-IF.

GROW-BUFFER.
    COMPUTE NEW-CAPACITY = CAPACITY * 2
    IF NEW-CAPACITY > 999999999
        DISPLAY "sequence too long" UPON SYSERR
        MOVE 1 TO RETURN-CODE
        STOP RUN
    END-IF
    SET OLD-PTR TO SEQ-PTR
    SET ADDRESS OF OLD-BUF TO OLD-PTR
    ALLOCATE NEW-CAPACITY CHARACTERS RETURNING SEQ-PTR
    SET ADDRESS OF SEQ-BUF TO SEQ-PTR
    IF SEQ-LEN > 0
        MOVE OLD-BUF(1:SEQ-LEN) TO SEQ-BUF(1:SEQ-LEN)
    END-IF
    FREE OLD-PTR
    MOVE NEW-CAPACITY TO CAPACITY.

FLUSH-SEQUENCE.
    DISPLAY HEADER-TEXT(1:HEADER-LEN)
    IF SEQ-LEN > 0
        INSPECT SEQ-BUF(1:SEQ-LEN) CONVERTING
            "ABCDGHKMNRSTUVWYabcdghkmnrstuvwy" TO
            "TVGHCDMKNYSAABWRTVGHCDMKNYSAABWR"
    END-IF
    MOVE SEQ-LEN TO START-POS
    PERFORM UNTIL START-POS < 60
        SUBTRACT 60 FROM START-POS
        MOVE FUNCTION REVERSE(SEQ-BUF(START-POS + 1:60)) TO OUT-LINE
        DISPLAY OUT-LINE
    END-PERFORM
    IF START-POS > 0
        MOVE START-POS TO TAIL-LEN
        MOVE FUNCTION REVERSE(SEQ-BUF(1:TAIL-LEN)) TO OUT-LINE
        DISPLAY OUT-LINE(1:TAIL-LEN)
    END-IF.
